# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets header rules (public/_headers).
#
# FIX 2026-11-10 (Phase 6, front-look fix #1) — explicit Content-Type rules.
#
# LIVE EVIDENCE (2026-11-10 ~00:15 IST, curl against formzalo.com):
# 9 of 33 files under /assets/* and every unchanged file at the site root
# (templates/*.png, og.jpg, favicon.svg, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, llms.txt)
# are served with NO Content-Type header at all, even though the files exist
# and return 200 with the correct bytes. Only files re-uploaded by the
# 2026-11-09 wrangler deploy (the 25 changed chunks + ads.txt) carry a
# Content-Type — the rest kept the previous (8 Nov, manual/API) upload's
# metadata, which has none, and wrangler's content-hash dedup never
# re-uploads unchanged files, so the bad metadata survives every deploy.
#
# A module script with no JavaScript MIME type is rejected by the browser's
# strict MIME check, so the dynamic import of the routes chunk fails with
# "Failed to fetch dynamically imported module: .../routes-DVImTrUA.js"
# — because its static dependency rolldown-runtime-C0FnF6B9.js (imported by
# EVERY route chunk) is one of the files served without a Content-Type.
# That is the whole homepage failure: the file exists, the loading path is
# broken. /faq, /templates and /services only *look* alive because their
# SSR HTML renders; their client JS is dead for the same reason.
#
# _headers rules override whatever the asset store has (Cloudflare docs:
# "Headers defined in the _headers file override what Cloudflare
# ordinarily sends"), and the existing /assets/* cache-control rule below
# is already visibly live on every asset response, which proves _headers
# IS applied to env.ASSETS.fetch() responses in this Worker. So these
# rules fix the MIME type at the asset-serving layer, independent of the
# stored upload metadata, and they survive future deploys unchanged.
/assets/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/assets/*.js
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8
/assets/*.mjs
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8
/assets/*.css
  Content-Type: text/css; charset=utf-8
/assets/*.png
  Content-Type: image/png
/assets/*.jpg
  Content-Type: image/jpeg
/assets/*.jpeg
  Content-Type: image/jpeg
/assets/*.svg
  Content-Type: image/svg+xml
/assets/*.webp
  Content-Type: image/webp
/assets/*.json
  Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
/assets/*.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
/assets/*.xml
  Content-Type: application/xml; charset=utf-8
/templates/*.png
  Content-Type: image/png
/og.jpg
  Content-Type: image/jpeg
/favicon.svg
  Content-Type: image/svg+xml
/robots.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
/sitemap.xml
  Content-Type: application/xml; charset=utf-8
/ads.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
/llms.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/assets/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*
  strict-transport-security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  x-content-type-options: nosniff
  referrer-policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
